WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.290
Enthusiastic Polar Bear.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:42.600
What's wrong, Panda?

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.080
Why are you sighing?

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.640
I don't want to go to work.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.290
That again?

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:53.840
There's nothing to do,
 so it's really boring.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.730
Even when I'm playing

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.070
"Hey, look over there" 
with Mr. Full-time Panda,

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.010
I get tired of it
 after fifteen minutes.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.120
I'm surprised you can even play 
that for fifteen minutes.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.520
I'd be sick of it after 
fifteen seconds.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:14.440
It's really hard to kill 
time, Mr. Penguin.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.710
I didn't have a choice, 
so I napped a bunch,

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:26.870
but I slept wrong and 
got a stiff neck.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.970
Even if I eat my snacks really slowly,

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.760
only a little bit of time passes.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.820
Ever since I started my 
part-time job as a panda,

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.500
I've been eating too many 
snacks and put on some weight.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.560
Again?

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.800
It's because of my job.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.520
You really think that's 
the only reason?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:51.060
Yup. I'm gaining weight 
because I have a job.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.570
You work at your job 
twice a week, right?

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.360
Yup.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:58.610
Stop complaining about having 
to work twice a week.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.660
Try working every day.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.350
You're right.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.950
I know.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.120
Maybe I'll make it once a week.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.610
You're making it even less?

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.750
It must be nice.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:16.280
I'm very busy at work. 
I'd like a little more free time.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:17.630
Really?

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.050
I'd like to have a change 
of pace once in a while.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.330
The café is rather busy.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.680
Jeez, it must be nice to be so busy.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.020
I want to be like you, Panda, 
and just laze around.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.740
Come on, you two.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.060
You're asking for things you can't have.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.320
You should say something 
to them, Miss Sasako.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.520
Well...

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.490
I just got a great idea.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:48.930
What is it?

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.170
Do you want to trade places 
for a day, Panda?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:53.960
Huh?

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.670
I'll go to the zoo to work as a panda,

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.920
and you can manage things 
here at Polar Bear's Café.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.330
No, no, no, that's a bad idea.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.110
That's a great idea.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.570
You're really cool, Polar Bear.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.850
I've wanted to be like you just once.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.770
No, that's a bad idea.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.690
You think so?

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.830
Stop saying weird stuff, Polar Bear.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:25.990
Panda

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.700
Oh, good morning, Panda—

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:34.220
Er... you're not Panda...

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.480
I'm Panda!

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.010
Was this the way to the panda corner?

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.930
W-Wait a minute!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.800
You're Polar Bear, aren't you?

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.300
Oh, you can tell?

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.200
I'll be fine, Mr. Handa.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.720
The visitors can't tell the difference 
between different bears.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.370
What are you talking about?!

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:02.460
They'll know right away 
with you, Polar Bear!

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.320
You need to go home!

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.090
Wait a sec.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.640
What is it, Kirino?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.240
Mr. Full-time Panda is off 
today on paid leave.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.260
Which would mean...

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.170
The pandas 
are out 
today.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:21.130
<i>Mommy, the pandas are gone!</i>

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.310
Where's Panda, Polar Bear?

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.890
He's not coming today.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.490
Call him, this instant!

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:33.020
Even if I called him now, 
it'd be too late.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.150
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:46.730
T-Try not to make yourself 
too obvious, please.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:49.680
Okay! I'll do my best!

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.600
Hey, Panda!

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:56.710
I just got some 
tasty-looking bamboo grass,

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.500
so I thought I'd bring you some—

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:17.180
I'm Panda!

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.260
I couldn't stop thinking about it,
 so I came to look.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.950
I'm a panda.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.160
I think I may have a fever.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.590
Oh? Am I not cute?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.740
How strange...

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.410
<i>I knew this was a bad idea!</i>

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:50.070
<i>He doesn't look anything like a panda!</i>

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.490
That's a panda?

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.010
Something seems off.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.970
He seems too long, or something.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.730
Isn't he too big?

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.720
Well, this is the first time 
we've seen a panda in person,

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.820
so maybe that's what they look like.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.440
I know, but...

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.820
isn't that a polar bear's silhouette?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.110
Oh, no! Not good.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:10.360
Equip

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.900
Equip item.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.860
Equip

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.490
Equip

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.330
And then use an ability.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.240
Ability

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.240
Ability

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.240
Panda Sit

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.240
Yes

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.830
No

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.830
Ability

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.830
Yes

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.440
See! It is a panda!

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.090
Well, I'll be!

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.500
Mr. Panda!

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:29.520
He's so big!

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.220
<i>Good job, Polar Bear!</i>

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.500
Thank you.

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.970
Excuse me.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.890
Yes, I'll be right there!

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.350
<i>There really is nothing 
to do at this job.</i>

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.650
He's sure not doing much.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.780
That's to be expected, he's a panda.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:56.200
<i>Whoops! Service, service.</i>

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:00.540
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:04.320
<i>How exactly do you play with a tire?</i>

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.610
He seems troubled.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.670
What's wrong with Mr. Panda?

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:14.130
<i>Oh, no! Everyone's becoming suspicious!</i>

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.570
Um...

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.050
Hey, he's playing!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.300
What the heck was that?

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:44.290
<i>No!</i>

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.250
<i>You're making everyone suspicious 
by doing unthinkable moves!</i>

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.020
Seeing a panda in person 
is totally different!

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:51.720
Yeah!

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.060
<i>What?!</i>

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:54.730
<i>Safe!</i>

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.180
<i>All right, I'll give them 
even more service.</i>

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.120
Whoa! It's a polar bear!

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.180
Hey.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:11.230
Whoa! It's a panda!

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:13.940
Whoa! It's a polar bear!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.870
Hey.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.570
Whoa! It's a panda!

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.050
Whoa! It's a polar bear!

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.950
Whoa! It's a panda!

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:22.660
Whoa! It's a polar bear!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:26.730
<i>P-P-Polar Bear!</i>

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:32.340
The pandas not being here isn't good.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.800
I'll be in trouble if people find out 
that Polar Bear isn't a panda.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.800
Maybe I should get an 
apology letter ready...

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.060
Mr. Handa, we've got a problem!

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:45.770
It's finally happened!

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.470
They've found out!

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:49.670
Polar Bear panda is a hit!

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:50.140
What do I do?!

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:50.980
Huh?

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:05.570
Got it.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:10.160
Amazing! He made it from that distance!

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.000
He could probably enter the Masters!

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:14.710
Thank you. Thank you.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.230
You're so amazing, Mr. Panda!

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.680
The panda merchandise is 
selling like crazy!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.270
Could I get this panda T-shirt?

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.890
I'd like all three colors 
of the panda handbags!

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.640
Mr. Handa!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.610
It's working beautifully!

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.370
Now that I think about it,

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.600
I wonder how it's going 
on the other end.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.040
Hello.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.500
Welcome.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.030
I wonder what I should get.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:00.070
Let's see...

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:06.290
Aren't you a little short 
to be a polar bear?

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.440
Or rather...

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.210
You're Panda, aren't you?

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:15.990
No, I'm Polar Bear.

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:20.970
Where did Polar Bear go?

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.850
I'm right here.

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:25.420
Well, that didn't fool them.

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:27.220
Indeed.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:33.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:32.160
Let's go to the beach!

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:37.480
Welcome.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:41.380
Huh? Where's Polar Bear today?

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:43.720
He's out for the day.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.920
Here we are, the beach!

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:55.270
The beach!

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.980
You've gotta head 
to the beach in summer.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.790
What do you think, Mr. Penguin?

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:02.740
This is a new shirt.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.020
But you don't usually 
wear clothes, Panda.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:09.090
I wanted to fit in with the setting.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:10.870
And what setting would that be?

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.830
Let's get changed and go swimming already.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:18.340
Let's relax a little, Polar Bear.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:20.790
Huh?

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:23.260
It's a panda!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.570
That it is.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.390
Imagine that. A panda at the beach.

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:29.140
Look at how cute he is 
in his Hawaiian shirt.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.920
Where ya headed?

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.970
How's 'bout a candy?

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:34.610
Thanks.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:36.970
See y'all again!

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:38.910
Y'all be careful!

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.880
I'm so popular.

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.120
Huh? Where's Polar Bear?

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.110
Over there.

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:46.010
You're so amazing!

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:47.540
So cool!

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.300
He's so popular.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:55.580
If we don't get in soon, 
it's going to get dark, Polar Bear!

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:59.440
You were just saying 
you wanted to relax.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:12.310
Ocean Breeze House

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.490
Tada!

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:05.110
So, you did change.

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.590
Don't you get tired of

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.900
always looking the same, Mr. Penguin?

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:12.310
You pretty much always look 
the same, too, Panda.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:15.060
What should we do first?

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.520
I'm gonna go fishing.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.480
I'm gonna take a nap.

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:26.910
What a great wave.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.870
Everyone's doing their own thing.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.040
Since we all came here together,

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.080
let's all do something together!

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.380
I heard they rent out 
kayaks over there.

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:44.930
What's that?

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.840
I don't know what it is, 
but I wanna do it!

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.770
Horizon as far as the eye can see.
 This is great!

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:58.710
This is hard, Polar Bear!

00:13:58.710 --> 00:13:59.730
How do you do this?

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:03.920
Without subermerging the paddle too deeply,

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.070
you pull with your dominant hand

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.450
and push with the opposite hand 
at the same time.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.480
Don't let your elbows break the plane above your shoulders.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:12.950
Instead, move your lower back―

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.390
Could you explain it 
more simply, please?!

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:17.870
Just paddle like you usually swim.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.830
All right!

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.470
Hey, did you see that, Panda?

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:28.130
I'm bored with this.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:28.720
Already?!

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:33.280
All you can see is the ocean 
and this thing isn't moving.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.850
Well we're in the ocean and

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.950
of course it's not moving 
since you aren't paddling!

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.360
Wanna try something you 
don't have to paddle?

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:52.070
What should we do next?

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:55.910
I wanna laze around on the beach.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.090
I'm going to leisurely dry some fish.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:00.040
I'm going to play the ukulele.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.560
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:27.530
Hey, build me a body.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:29.440
What type of body?

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:33.740
I want to look macho and sexy.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.200
Like your previous upside-down triangle 
body with the long legs?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:40.160
<i>I've been called, so here 
I am, the Dream Panda!</i>

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:43.210
Something a little more tough than that,

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:45.340
but not too muscular.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:46.630
You're being really picky.

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:48.740
Leave it to me.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.060
How's that?

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:53.790
He's totally a sumo wrestler.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.110
He's tough, but not too muscular.

00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:57.560
No!

00:15:58.370 --> 00:15:59.600
Leave it to me.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:03.410
This is too tough.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:06.070
I want to look cooler.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:08.070
Leave it to me.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:13.240
This is cool, but not what 
I was thinking of.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.700
I want to be popular!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:15.990
Leave it to me.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.570
Will I be popular?

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:25.550
Yes. Everyone's celebrating your glory.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.330
Am I really needed in this?

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:30.630
What should we do next?

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.190
Who's going first?

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:36.800
You should go, Polar Bear.

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:39.260
You sure?

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:41.980
Why are you hesitating?

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.150
I'm not hesitating, it's just...

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:53.840
I know where it is even 
when I'm blindfolded.

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.340
My sense of smell is really good.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.830
Then you go, Panda.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.590
All right!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:07.280
Panda? Are you asleep?

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:10.250
Apparently blindfolding 
Panda is a bad idea.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.560
To your right, Mr. Penguin!

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:20.140
Huh?! How far to the right?!

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.270
Turn your upper body to 
the right 30 degrees,

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.600
and then slightly bend 
your body forward.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.860
Then raise your arms 
to about eye level...

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:29.820
Would you explain more simply?!

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.300
Right in front of you.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.530
Right there, Mr. Penguin!

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.150
Really?

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:39.450
Imagine you're going after Miss Penko!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.010
Miss Penko, um...

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:48.600
D-Do you like dried fish, Miss Penko?

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.080
I love them!

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:54.090
I also love them, but, Miss Penko, I...

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.850
I... Miss Penko!

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.580
Miss Penko!

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:06.720
Mish Fenko! Will you hear 
meh out? Mish Fenko!

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:09.900
Mish Fenko! Mish Fenko!

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:08.790
May you two live happily.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:16.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.170
Are you ready to order?

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.610
A large serving of bamboo!

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:28.850
We don't have that.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:30.830
Then a normal serving is just fine.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:34.050
I'm sorry, we don't have either.

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:38.050
Beach house special: 
large serving of bamboo.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:40.190
It'll be a hit.

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:41.760
Just for you, Panda.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.220
Salmon Yakisoba

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:48.690
I'll have the lightly smoked salmon 
mie cuit with sauce cressonnière.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:49.560
That's not it.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:53.240
I'll have that, too, with bamboo topping.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.940
They don't have that topping.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.400
What about you, Mr. Penguin?

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:02.120
Huh? I'll have the seafood ramen.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.690
Ow! Hot, hot, hot!

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:10.500
Mr. Penguin does always eat raw fish.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:12.290
He's got a penguin's tongue.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:14.750
What do you mean?

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.460
The penguin version of a cat's tongue.

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:20.400
Saying I have a cat's 
tongue would be fine!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:22.520
You can do it.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.840
The seafood is waiting 
for you, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:30.240
You should eat seafood in the ocean.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:35.230
Could you not state the obvious?

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:38.550
Hey, that's bad manners.

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:40.200
Girls won't like you.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:42.660
See?

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:44.150
Huh?

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.320
Mr. Panda's eating yakisoba!

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:48.830
How cute!

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:50.980
Very well-liked.

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:52.190
Why?

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:54.540
Because I'm one with the setting.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.770
But I'm eating ramen, too.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.840
Whoa! That penguin is eating ramen!

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.010
What's up with that? 
So weird!

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:08.050
Not well-liked.

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:09.480
Why?!

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:19.860
Isn't this good?

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:29.040
Maybe there's a setting that 
makes things delicious.

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:33.500
Sitting here with everyone, 
feeling the wind...

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:34.680
Huh?

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:37.210
Let's eat some shaved ice next.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.060
I want strawberry flavored.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:42.170
I was saying something really good!

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.730
Jeez, we all got different things.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:50.330
Everyone's so selfish.

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:53.130
No teamwork whatsoever.

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:54.600
We're all disorganized.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:06.370
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:37.320
That was fun, wasn't it?

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:40.150
It was. And I was able 
to make dried fish.

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:44.110
The beach sure is great.

00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:06.510
This ends our daily train schedule.

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:08.970
We overslept.

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:11.970
The mountains are a great place, too.

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.470
What should we do next?

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:17.170
Want some dried fish?

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:24.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.570
Next Time

00:23:58.150 --> 00:23:59.870
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:01.080
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.770
It's hard to think of something 
fun to talk about

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:12.050
Studio Pierrot

00:24:03.770 --> 00:24:05.970
when you're talking to someone 
you're not interested in.

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:08.230
Could you not announce that to me?

00:24:08.230 --> 00:24:11.050
Then show me one of your best 
impersonations of Polar Bear.

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:12.050
What?!

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:13.760
Next time on Polar Bear's Café—

00:24:13.620 --> 00:24:14.960
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:14.960 --> 00:24:15.760
What?!

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:17.700
Next time, Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:19.790
will air at 5:30 AM.

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:24.480
Studio Pierrot

00:24:19.790 --> 00:24:21.840
PM! 5:30 PM!

00:24:20.710 --> 00:24:24.480
Weeding in the Summer

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:23.180
Enjoy!
